   "source": [
    "# Justification Codes\n",
    "\n",
    "To place plot embellishments, such as scalebars, directional roses, colorbars, legends,\n",
    "text, or images on a figure, two points have to be specified: a point somewhere on the\n",
    "figure (**reference point**) and a point on the feature (**anchor point**). For both,\n",
    "users can use a two-character code, a combination of a vertical code and a horizontal\n",
    "code (order-independent):\n",
    "\n",
    "- Vertical: **T** (Top), **M** (Middle), **B** (Bottom)\n",
    "- Horizontal: **L** (Left), **C** (Centre), **R** (Right)\n",
    "\n",
    "For example, `\"TL\"` means **T**op **L**eft.\n",
    "\n",
    "The possible nine justification codes are visualized in the sketch below:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "9c69525b",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "remove-input"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {
      "image/png": {
       "width": 600
      }
     },
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "Script showing the justification codes used in GMT / PyGMT.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "import pygmt\n",
    "\n",
    "size = 5\n",
    "x1 = [-size, 0, size, size, size, 0, -size, -size, 0]\n",
    "y1 = [-size, -size, -size, 0, size, size, size, 0, 0]\n",
    "codes = [\"BL\", \"BC\", \"BR\", \"MR\", \"TR\", \"TC\", \"TL\", \"ML\", \"MC\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "fig = pygmt.Figure()\n",
    "fig.basemap(projection=\"X10c/6c\", region=[-size, size, -size, size], frame=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.text(\n",
    "    font=\"15p,1,black\",\n",
    "    x=x1,\n",
    "    y=y1,\n",
    "    text=codes,\n",
    "    justify=codes,\n",
    "    offset=\"j0.5c/0.5c+v2p,gray30\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.plot(x=x1, y=y1, style=\"c0.3c\", fill=\"steelblue\", no_clip=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.text(\n",
    "    font=\"15p\",\n",
    "    offset=\"j0.5c/0.5c\",\n",
    "    no_clip=True,\n",
    "    x=[size, size, size, -size, 0, size],\n",
    "    y=[size, 0, -size, size, size, size],\n",
    "    justify=[\"ML\", \"ML\", \"ML\", \"BC\", \"BC\", \"BC\"],\n",
    "    text=[\n",
    "        \"@%1%T@%%op\",\n",
    "        \"@%1%M@%%iddle\",\n",
    "        \"@%1%B@%%ottom\",\n",
    "        \"@%1%L@%%eft\",\n",
    "        \"@%1%C@%%enter\",\n",
    "        \"@%1%R@%%ight\",\n",
    "    ],\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.show(width=600)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a76963ad",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "For a non-rectangular geographic basemap, the justification codes refer to the invisible,\n",
    "rectangular map bounding box:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "e3c71bd4",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "remove-input"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {
      "image/png": {
       "width": 600
      }
     },
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "Script showing justification codes for non-rectangular geographic basemaps.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "fig = pygmt.Figure()\n",
    "fig.basemap(projection=\"H10c\", region=\"g\", frame=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "for code in codes:\n",
    "    fig.text(\n",
    "        font=\"10p,1,black\",\n",
    "        position=code,\n",
    "        justify=code,\n",
    "        text=code,\n",
    "        offset=\"j0.5c/0.5c+v2p,gray30\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    fig.text(font=\"10p,steelblue\", position=code, justify=\"MC\", text=\"●\", no_clip=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.show(width=600)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "435af604",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Plot embellishments can be abstracted as rectangles. Here, the justification codes are\n",
    "shown exemplary for a colorbar."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "b743a12d",
   "metadata": {
    "tags": [
     "remove-input"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Image object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {
      "image/png": {
       "width": 600
      }
     },
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "Script showing justification codes for plot embellishments, e.g., a colorbar.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "fig = pygmt.Figure()\n",
    "fig.basemap(projection=\"X10c/2c\", region=[-size, size, -size, size], frame=0)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.colorbar(\n",
    "    cmap=\"SCM/hawaii\",\n",
    "    frame=0,\n",
    "    position=\"MC\",\n",
    "    length=10,\n",
    "    width=2,\n",
    "    orientation=\"horizontal\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "for code in codes:\n",
    "    fig.text(\n",
    "        font=\"10p,1,black\",\n",
    "        position=code,\n",
    "        justify=code,\n",
    "        text=code,\n",
    "        offset=\"j0.3c/0.15c+v1p,gray30\",\n",
    "    )\n",
    "fig.plot(x=x1, y=y1, style=\"c0.2c\", fill=\"steelblue\", no_clip=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.show(width=600)"
   ]
  }
